                <pb facs="1093" n="999" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg999"/>

                <head>No. 626.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Strobel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 20,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 228.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from Havana, on the subject of new passport regulations for Americans,
                    as contained in the royal order of July 30 last.</p>
                <p>The Department suspends any expression of opinion on the new rules until their
                    practical working shall be better known.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>





